<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <!-- Distributed from 0.4.0. It was held back as spike-stage from Phase 316, which had
         the effect that no domain workspace could consume the engine at all — the one
         domain using it reached across a sibling checkout for a byte-copy of its output.
         The engine is domain-generic by construction (a vocabulary is a plain `Idl` value
         a caller supplies), so shipping it is what makes a second vocabulary declarable
         without the declarer living in this repo. See DECISIONS.md D14.

         Split from the codegen half at 0.7.0 (Phase 97, DECISIONS.md D17): this package is
         the model, the codec, the sampler and the sanitisation floor — values in, values
         out — and is Fable-clean, gated by `tests/fable-smoke`. The source emitters and the
         diff classifier ship beside it as `Fuaran.Core.Idl.Codegen`, whose real contract is
         the shape of what it EMITS. A consumer that wants to decode a tree or sample a
         vocabulary no longer takes a generator's output cadence to do it. -->
    <IsPackable>true</IsPackable>
    <PackageId>Fuaran.Core.Idl</PackageId>
    <Description>Fuaran.Core.Idl — the interface-definition model: a typed description of a domain's node vocabulary (kinds, unions, enums, records, four-way optionality, a declarable node envelope, hosted slots), the schema-driven canonical encoder/decoder derived from it, a deterministic adversarial sampler over a vocabulary, the canonical `idl.json` artifact projection, and the host-neutral sanitisation floor. Fable-clean on both the encode and the decode path. The source emitters (F#, TypeScript, JSON Schema), the codegen trust boundary and the stability diff classifier ship separately as Fuaran.Core.Idl.Codegen. The engine only; a vocabulary is DATA a domain declares and owns in its own repo. FSharp.Core + Fuaran.Core.Wire only.</Description>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <Compile Include="Idl.fs" />
    <Compile Include="Sanitize.fs" />
    <Compile Include="Sample.fs" />
    <Compile Include="Artifact.fs" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Fuaran.Core.Wire\Fuaran.Core.Wire.fsproj" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="FSharp.Core" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
